-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
THIRD-PARTY OPEN DATA & CARTOGRAPHIC ATTRIBUTION NOTICE
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
While the client-side application source code (`index.html`, `styles.css`,
`i18n.js`, `laos_data.js`, `api.js`, `app.js`, `start_tier1a.bat`) is licensed
under the MIT License above, live hydrometeorological, satellite, radar, and
map tile streams accessed at runtime remain governed by their respective
upstream licenses and non-commercial terms of service:

1. Weather & Flood Forecast APIs:
   - Open-Meteo.com (https://open-meteo.com/) — Licensed under Attribution 4.0
     International (CC BY 4.0) for Non-Commercial use (ECMWF IFS, JMA GSM,
     DWD ICON, NOAA GFS, and Copernicus GloFAS v4.0).
2. River Discharge Ensemble:
   - Copernicus Emergency Management Service (CEMS) Global Flood Awareness
     System (GloFAS v4.0) — Model-derived river discharge (m3/s).
3. Geostationary Satellite Imagery:
   - NASA Global Imagery Browse Services (GIBS) WMTS — JMA Himawari-9 AHI
     (Band 13 Clean IR 10.4 um, Band 3 Red Visible, Air Mass RGB).
4. Weather Radar Composite:
   - RainViewer Public Weather Maps API (https://www.rainviewer.com/api.html) —
     Past 2-hour composite reflectivity tiles up to Zoom Level 7.
5. Regional Surface Synoptic Charts:
   - Thai Meteorological Department (TMD, https://www.tmd.go.th/) and
     Hydro-Informatics Institute (HII ThaiWater, https://tiwrm.hii.or.th/).
6. Basemap Vector & Raster Tiles:
   - OpenFreeMap (https://openfreemap.org/) and CARTO Basemaps, using data
     (c) OpenStreetMap contributors under the Open Database License (ODbL).
